I do feel that "to say" and "to talk" are distinct, but you asked for
"sayer" and "talker". "Sayer" doesn't mean anything to me (except in
"soothsayer", "truthsayer", and probably other compounds), whereas "talker"
is a common word. So they're still distinct, but for different reasons.
And no, I didn't realize you were talking only about flashcards. I have no
interest in the flashcard project, so I don't want to influence it either
way.

stevo

